List<String> chapterFour = [
  '- Petition for the Acceptance of a Candidate for the Conveyance of Gold -\n\nLet this matter be entrusted unto me, and let the burden of this gold be placed upon my hands.',
  'For the place wherein it now rests is no longer secure, and the eyes of many have turned toward it. Therefore it is wise that it be removed swiftly and with prudence, before harm befalls it.',
  'The men who journey with me are seasoned in the secret conveyance of precious things. They are silent as the waters of a deep well, and swift as the birds that pass over the mountains. They leave no trace upon the road, nor do they draw the attention of thieves and idle watchers.',
  'Though the desert be wide and the paths uncertain, we know its ways. We travel by the signs of the heavens and by the wisdom gained from many journeys. Neither the burning sun nor the cold of the night shall turn us aside from our charge.',
  'If this trust be given unto me, the treasure shall pass unseen through the wilderness and shall arrive safely at the place appointed for it.',
  'May wisdom guide your judgment in this matter, and may peace be upon all who labor for the preservation of what is precious.',
];